      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "NOVAToken on BNB Chain was exploited on 2022-12-09 when the attacker address 0xcbf184b8156e1271449cfb42a7d0556a8dcfef72 called rewardHolders on the token contract, a path public notes describe as malicious unlimited minting. The exact net loss is not reconciled in the available record. A caller-controlled rewardHolders(uint256) path functioned as an unlimited mint or reward creation mechanism. The attacker supplied an enormous amount value, the transaction succeeded, and public incident notes describe the result as a mint followed by a swap into BNB. The retrieved evidence does not include the historical contract source, so the exact missing guard or modifier remains unverified."
